  "summary": "Sun Prairie, WI will not renew its Flock Safety ALPR contract on Dec. 31 and is considering Axon as a replacement to consolidate vendors, with plans to revise data retention and sharing policies. A public hearing is scheduled for Oct. 7, and a resident quoted in the story questions the need for the cameras.",
  "key_quotes": [
    {
      "quote": "Sun Prairie will not renew its contract with Flock Safety on Dec. 31 and is considering Axon as a potential replacement for its license plate reader cameras.",
      "paragraph_idx": 6
    },
    {
      "quote": "We're going to start from scratch, and we're going to work our way with what we think is right",
      "paragraph_idx": 9
    },
    {
      "quote": "Three cameras were added specifically around Woodman's and the dialysis center over there, which means anyone going to that place cannot get there by vehicle without being tracked by these cameras",
      "paragraph_idx": 10
    }
  ],
